ravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-02T15:29:25Z","updated_at":"2026-06-02T15:29:25Z","body":"Clicking on the members overview should still center to the line even if the caret is on the line, since you may have scrolled out of view.\r\nI don't think making it toggle fold is very useful or expected. Does any other IDE do this? \r\nFolding is unrelated to what shows in the members overview, it doesn't show all foldable lines and it may show non-foldable lines.\r\nThere are multiple ways to toggle folding already, we don't need to add it here as well. After clicking on the member overview you can use the toggle fold button in the gutter or the shortcut or the menu.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4603983173/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604135848","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119957#issuecomment-4604135848","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119957","id":4604135848,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEm2JqA","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-02T15:46:26Z","updated_at":"2026-06-02T15:46:26Z","body":"> I don't think making it toggle fold is very useful or expected. Does any other IDE do this?\r\n\r\nBoth VSCode and IntelliJ seem to unfold the relevant sections when navigating from the structure/outline view.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604135848/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604511937","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119957#issuecomment-4604511937","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119957","id":4604511937,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEnNGwQ","user":{"login":"SOEL86","id":4308535,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMDg1MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4308535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86","html_url":"https://github.com/SOEL86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-02T16:31:01Z","updated_at":"2026-06-02T16:39:07Z","body":"> Clicking on the members overview should still center to the line even if the caret is on the line\r\n\r\nI agree with that. I am looking into it. I need to find the mechanism goto_line_centered uses to center the caret.\r\n\r\nRegarding the single expected behaviour argument: It's a lot of screen space for a not very useful function. I usually hide it. Most people just scroll until they recognise the code. The new feature trains you to look at the member overview first, and peek at the function only long enough to decide if it's the one you need. I find it reduces 'overwhelm' significantly.\r\n\r\nEdit: RE: Multiple ways exist already: In fact, there is only one consistently functioning way to fold a function and that's by clicking the arrow. Alt + F is shared by another UI element in the editor. Besides, the existing ways are less convenient.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604511937/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604760849","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119957#issuecomment-4604760849","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119957","id":4604760849,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEncTEQ","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-02T16:56:40Z","updated_at":"2026-06-02T16:58:59Z","body":"> > I don't think making it toggle fold is very useful or expected. Does any other IDE do this?\r\n> \r\n> Both VSCode and IntelliJ seem to unfold the relevant sections when navigating from the structure/outline view.\r\n\r\nThis is the same behavior Godot currently has, it unfolds when jumping to the line. (Though VSCode only unfolds when the line is hidden, not folded)\r\nThis PR is about folding when clicking it again, which no other IDEs do as far I can tell.\r\n\r\n> Regarding the single expected behaviour argument: It's a lot of screen space for a not very useful function. I usually hide it. Most people just scroll until they recognise the code. The new feature trains you to look at the member overview first, and peek at the function only long enough to decide if it's the one you need. I find it reduces 'overwhelm' significantly.\r\n\r\nI still don't see how this helps, just using the member overview normally without this feature allows you to jump to functions immediately to let you decide if you are looking for it and you can just click the next function in the list. Folding doesn't help using the member overview to find a function, it just adds more clicks and makes it more complex.\r\nAdding folding here means you need to be more careful using it if you don't want to fold a function, it seems to me like it would train people to not use the member overview to find functions and to instead use it to fold/unfold lines. If people even find it, since it is not obvious that it would fold the line.\r\nAnd about screen space, it can be hidden if unwanted but it only takes space from the open document list which ideally shouldn't be too long anyway (for performance reasons).\r\n\r\nThe shortcut conflict can be rebound or removed in Editor Settings. Also see https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101104","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604760849/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604835247","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119957#issuecomment-4604835247","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119957","id":4604835247,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEng1rw","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-02T17:02:44Z","updated_at":"2026-06-02T17:02:44Z","body":"> This PR is about folding when clicking it again, which no other IDEs do as far I can tell.\r\n\r\nMy bad, I misread.\r\n\r\nFor a double click my intuitive action would be selecting the range of the item. But we don't have the technical foundation for that afaik.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4604835247/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4606279427","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119957#issuecomment-4606279427","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119957","id":4606279427,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEo4_Aw","user":{"login":"SOEL86","id":4308535,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzMDg1MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4308535?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SOEL86","html_url":"https://github.com/SOEL86","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/use